# Guides refresh workflow

When the user asks to complete/update **guides** (e.g. "completar guías", "dos videos"):

## Written guides

1. Search the web for useful, **current** guide topics per active game hub.
2. Read existing `src/content/articles/*.md` with `category: guide` — avoid duplicates.
3. Add **1–2** new `category: guide` articles per game unless the user specifies otherwise.
4. Use recent `publishedAt` dates; lists sort **newest first** automatically.
5. Cozy magazine tone (`docs/EDITORIAL.md`); step-by-step but not optimizer-speak.
6. Use `coverImage` + optional inline `<figure class="article-inline-figure">` when helpful.

## Video guides (two per game)

- Curate **2 YouTube videos per active game** on `src/data/game-video-guides.ts`.
- Each entry: `slug`, `title`, `gameSlug`, `youtubeId`, `channel`, `summary`, `tags[]`, optional `publishedAt` (YYYY-MM-DD).
- List **newest first** (`publishedAt` desc); `getVideoGuidesByGame` sorts automatically.
- Prefer recent, clear walkthroughs; verify the video ID loads on YouTube.
- Videos render on `/{game}/guides` via `IslandTourCard` (new tab, 3-column grid).
- NTE may keep older evergreen videos; swap or add when 1.x content ships.

## Verify

- `npm run content:lint`
- Do not commit unless asked.
